src/lbfgsb.rs ports scipy 1.18.1 scipy/optimize/src/lbfgsb.c, the C translation
of L-BFGS-B 3.0 that scipy ships under the licence above. L-BFGS-B 3.0 is by
Ciyou Zhu in collaboration with R. H. Byrd, P. Lu-Chen and J. Nocedal, with the
3.0 changes by Jose Luis Morales and Jorge Nocedal. It was released under the
BSD licence; its authors ask users to cite the papers. The references, as
lbfgsb.c gives them:

  [1] R. H. Byrd, P. Lu, J. Nocedal and C. Zhu, "A limited memory algorithm
      for bound constrained optimization", SIAM J. Scientific Computing 16
      (1995), no. 5, pp. 1190-1208.

  [2] C. Zhu, R. H. Byrd, P. Lu, J. Nocedal, "L-BFGS-B: FORTRAN Subroutines for
      Large Scale Bound Constrained Optimization", Tech. Report, NAM-11, EECS
      Department, Northwestern University, 1994.

  [3] J. L. Morales, J. Nocedal, "Remark On Algorithm 788: L-BFGS-B: Fortran
      Subroutines for Large-Scale Bound Constrained Optimization", 2011.

The line search routines dcsrch and dcstep come from MINPACK-1 and MINPACK-2
(Jorge J. More and David J. Thuente; Brett M. Averick, Richard G. Carter and
Jorge J. More), as scipy includes them under its licence.

